  "skill_summaries": {
    "ultimate": "heal and buff allies within range",
    "skill1": "heal one ally over time",
    "skill2": "AoE burst damages foes and heals allies",
    "skill3": "combat max HP increase",
    "skill4": "battle-start heal and buff the ally on tile in front",
    "skill5": "low HP ally triggers emergency heal"
  },
  "play_overview": "[[Fay]] heals and buffs allies within ultimate range, combining steady single-target healing with an area burst that damages foes while healing friends. She opens by healing and buffing the ally in front of her tile, and combat max HP rises over time. Low-HP allies can trigger an emergency heal for clutch saves. She is a reliable early support when stronger healers are unavailable. Her healing and buffs remain modest compared with top supports, so she needs a carry who converts them into pressure.",
  "counter_overview": "[[Fay]] is a modest healer and buffer whose battle-start heal, HoT, and area splash keep a nearby carry upright. The carry she supports is the real threat, not [[Fay]] alone. Outpace the sustain by racing your own carry with [[filter:energy-provider]] like [[Thador]] or [[Hugin]], or delete that partner with [[filter:assassin-delete]] like [[Ravion]] or [[Himmel]]. Do not spend a full anti-heal package only for [[Fay]] when her numbers are already modest."
}
